🛡️ DVWA_SQL_INJECTION

🔍 Project Description:
This practical demonstrates SQL Injection testing using the Damn Vulnerable Web Application (DVWA) in a controlled local lab environment. The objective was to understand how improperly validated user input can affect database queries and potentially expose unauthorized information. 🧪

💻 Tools & Environment: DVWA, Docker, Ubuntu, Kali Linux, VirtualBox, and Burp Suite.

🎯 Testing: Configured DVWA to Low security level and tested SQL Injection using crafted input to observe the application's response.

📚 Key Learning: Learned the fundamentals of SQL Injection, input manipulation, vulnerability identification, and the importance of secure input validation and parameterized queries. 🔐
